  "latestTerminalSummary": "Confirmed at `9f50d043`, using installed MCP SDK **1.32.1**. Read-only; no builds, tests, or probe rerun.\n\nThe false “unsent” result is real. The probe applies the comment before releasing the later ping, yet records `superseded: true` with an “unsent” limitation ([probe:34](/tmp/taskbot140-review-r5/ambiguous-protocol-probe.mjs:34), [receipt:63–74](/tmp/taskbot140-review-r5/ambiguous-protocol-probe.json:63)). The current guard covers every POST/send while `invoking`, captures errors even after awaiting the write result, then replaces the operation error with shared `declined` ([implementation:87–153](/Users/jappy/.t3/worktrees/bobs-factory/taskbot-140-views/packages/mcp-tools/src/callConfiguredTool.ts:87)).\n\nRecommend a minimal per-request guard:\n\n- Bind authority **out of band to the exact SDK-generated outbound `tools/call` envelope**. Wrap every `transport.send`; explicitly clear mutation scope for replies and notifications. AsyncLocalStorage can carry scope through SDK preparation, with exact envelope correlation at fetch.\n- HTTP/SSE: retain `dispatch.run(() => fetch(...))` at each matching actual POST, including redirects/retransmissions, **after async preparation**. Stdio: guard only the matching synchronous send.\n- Remove shared `declined`; preserve the original operation result/error. Track write invocation inside the guarded callback. `UnsentDispatchError` is valid only before any mutation write starts; refusal after an earlier attempt must remain uncertain.\n- Keep arguments unchanged. Nested `method`, `id`, `_meta`, or dispatch-like data must neither grant authority nor bypass validation. ID equality alone is insufficient.\n\n+++Installed SDK source proof\n\nPaths below are under `packages/mcp-tools/node_modules/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/dist/esm/`.\n\n- **Request/control framing:** `Client.callTool` creates `method: \"tools/call\"`; Protocol generates its ID. Automatic ping replies send `{result, jsonrpc, id}`; abort/timeout sends `notifications/cancelled` with `params.requestId`. These are separate frames despite correlated IDs. Incoming response IDs are normalized with `Number(response.id)`. Proof: [client/index.js:479](/Users/jappy/.t3/worktrees/bobs-factory/taskbot-140-views/packages/mcp-tools/node_modules/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/dist/esm/client/index.js:479), [shared/protocol.js:665](/Users/jappy/.t3/worktrees/bobs-factory/taskbot-140-views/packages/mcp-tools/node_modules/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/dist/esm/shared/protocol.js:665), [ping reply:401](/Users/jappy/.t3/worktrees/bobs-factory/taskbot-140-views/packages/mcp-tools/node_modules/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/dist/esm/shared/protocol.js:401), [correlation:477](/Users/jappy/.t3/worktrees/bobs-factory/taskbot-140-views/packages/mcp-tools/node_modules/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/dist/esm/shared/protocol.js:477).\n\n- **HTTP writes/redirects:** `send` awaits headers, serializes JSON, then calls injected fetch. Default redirects use manual fetch and re-enter that fetch for up to five method-preserving hops: POST follows 307/308 within origin, including the defined default-port HTTP→HTTPS upgrade. Cross-origin, added userinfo, and POST 301/302/303 are refused. Proof: [streamableHttp.js:302](/Users/jappy/.t3/worktrees/bobs-factory/taskbot-140-views/packages/mcp-tools/node_modules/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/dist/esm/client/streamableHttp.js:302), [shared/transport.js:39–91](/Users/jappy/.t3/worktrees/bobs-factory/taskbot-140-views/packages/mcp-tools/node_modules/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/dist/esm/shared/transport.js:39).\n\n- **Auth/retries:** HTTP can resend the same message after 401 authentication or 403 insufficient-scope authentication; legacy SSE retries after 401. **Current caller supplies no `authProvider`**, so these branches are inactive. OAuth POSTs must remain separate if enabled later. Proof: [HTTP:328](/Users/jappy/.t3/worktrees/bobs-factory/taskbot-140-views/packages/mcp-tools/node_modules/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/dist/esm/client/streamableHttp.js:328), [SSE:172](/Users/jappy/.t3/worktrees/bobs-factory/taskbot-140-views/packages/mcp-tools/node_modules/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/dist/esm/client/sse.js:172).\n\n- **SSE/resumption:** Streamable HTTP reconnects through GET with Last-Event-ID, rather than replaying the POST. Legacy SSE receives individual messages through EventSource and POSTs to its same-origin advertised endpoint. Proof: [HTTP resumption:89](/Users/jappy/.t3/worktrees/bobs-factory/taskbot-140-views/packages/mcp-tools/node_modules/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/dist/esm/client/streamableHttp.js:89), [legacy SSE:77](/Users/jappy/.t3/worktrees/bobs-factory/taskbot-140-views/packages/mcp-tools/node_modules/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/dist/esm/client/sse.js:77).\n\n- **Stdio/batches:** Stdio synchronously writes `JSON.stringify(message) + \"\\n\"` once; backpressure waits for drain, with no resend. Streamable HTTP supports outbound batches and JSON response arrays; SSE event and stdio parsers accept individual messages. This caller generates one request. Never let a mixed batch containing the mutation bypass the guard. Proof: [stdio.js:179](/Users/jappy/.t3/worktrees/bobs-factory/taskbot-140-views/packages/mcp-tools/node_modules/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/dist/esm/client/stdio.js:179), [stdio framing:34](/Users/jappy/.t3/worktrees/bobs-factory/taskbot-140-views/packages/mcp-tools/node_modules/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/dist/esm/shared/stdio.js:34), [HTTP batches:394](/Users/jappy/.t3/worktrees/bobs-factory/taskbot-140-views/packages/mcp-tools/node_modules/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/dist/esm/client/streamableHttp.js:394).\n\n+++",
